      "parameters": {
        "descriptionType": "manual",
        "toolDescription": "Runs a MongoDB aggregation pipeline over the doc_rows collection to answer questions about tabular files (CSV, XLSX, Google Sheets). Use it for sums, averages, counts, maximums, or filtering rows.\n\nEvery document in doc_rows has this shape:\n{ \"file_id\": \"<the file_id from listDocuments>\", \"row_data\": { \"<column name>\": \"<value>\", ... } }\n\nColumn names come from the schema field in listDocuments. Values are stored as strings, so wrap numeric fields in $toDouble.\n\nAlways $match on file_id first. Pass the pipeline as a JSON array string.\n\nExample 1, average revenue:\n[{\"$match\": {\"file_id\": \"1AbC123\"}}, {\"$group\": {\"_id\": null, \"avg_revenue\": {\"$avg\": {\"$toDouble\": \"$row_data.revenue\"}}}}]\n\nExample 2, total sales per category:\n[{\"$match\": {\"file_id\": \"1AbC123\"}}, {\"$group\": {\"_id\": \"$row_data.category\", \"total_sales\": {\"$sum\": {\"$toDouble\": \"$row_data.sales\"}}}}, {\"$sort\": {\"total_sales\": -1}}]\n\nExample 3, first 20 rows:\n[{\"$match\": {\"file_id\": \"1AbC123\"}}, {\"$limit\": 20}, {\"$project\": {\"_id\": 0, \"row_data\": 1}}]",
        "operation": "aggregate",
        "collection": "doc_rows",
        "query": "={{ $fromAI('pipeline', 'A MongoDB aggregation pipeline as a JSON array string. Must start with a $match on file_id.') }}"
      },
